      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "summary": "What this topic covers.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "topic-map",
          "html": "<p>Most messages, emails and calls pass through a company's servers on the way. With ordinary SMS and email, that company &mdash; and anyone it hands data to &mdash; can read them. <b>End-to-end encrypted</b> apps like Signal mean only you and the person you're talking to can read the content, and email aliases stop your real address from spreading.</p>"
        }
      ]
